    {
     "type": "code",
     "lang": "python",
     "code": "import json\nuser = {\"name\": \"Sara\", \"admin\": False, \"pet\": None}\ntext = json.dumps(user)\nprint(text)\n# {\"name\": \"Sara\", \"admin\": false, \"pet\": null}\n\ndata = json.loads('{\"name\": \"Ali\", \"ok\": true}')\nprint(data[\"name\"])   # Ali\nprint(data)           # {'name': 'Ali', 'ok': True}",
     "highlight": [
      3,
      7
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "code",
     "lang": "python",
     "code": "print(json.dumps({\"name\": \"Sara\", \"langs\": [\"en\", \"ar\"]}, indent=2))\n# {\n#   \"name\": \"Sara\",\n#   \"langs\": [\n#     \"en\",\n#     \"ar\"\n#   ]\n# }",
     "highlight": [
      1
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "tip",
     "en": "The `s` means string: `dumps` = dump to string, `loads` = load from string. `indent=2` makes it pretty.",
     "ar": "الحرف `s` يعني نص (string): `dumps` = حوّل إلى نص، `loads` = اقرأ من نص. و`indent=2` يجعله مرتبًا."
    }
   ]
